From 715893e42af2eaf31768c7ea803dde9748aa08ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] IsEqual compares the space of far address translations

An IA_FARXLAT unary operator keeps its far space (and offset) in
mConst, so two translations of the same pointer into different spaces
compared equal and common-instruction merging kept one of them.
NetHack's doeat() read objects[otyp].oc_nutrition through the mons[]
space, so every food ration gave no nutrition and was eaten in one bite,
and the far heap's nh_halloc() read a free list link of the monster
heap from the object heap.

Both IsEqual() and IsEqualSource() now compare mConst for it, as they do
for constants and frame pushes and pops.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/InterCode.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/oscar64/InterCode.cpp b/oscar64/InterCode.cpp
index 818673e..c263e40 100644
--- a/oscar64/InterCode.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/InterCode.cpp
@@ -3089,7 +3089,7 @@ bool InterInstruction::IsEqual(const InterInstruction* ins) const
 		if (!mSrc[i].IsEqual(ins->mSrc[i]))
 			return false;
 
-	if ((mCode == IC_CONSTANT || mCode == IC_PUSH_FRAME || mCode == IC_POP_FRAME) && !mConst.IsEqual(ins->mConst))
+	if ((mCode == IC_CONSTANT || mCode == IC_PUSH_FRAME || mCode == IC_POP_FRAME || mOperator == IA_FARXLAT) && !mConst.IsEqual(ins->mConst))
 		return false;
 
 	return true;
@@ -3110,7 +3110,7 @@ bool InterInstruction::IsEqualSource(const InterInstruction* ins) const
 		if (!mSrc[i].IsEqual(ins->mSrc[i]))
 			return false;
 
-	if ((mCode == IC_CONSTANT || mCode == IC_PUSH_FRAME || mCode == IC_POP_FRAME) && !mConst.IsEqual(ins->mConst))
+	if ((mCode == IC_CONSTANT || mCode == IC_PUSH_FRAME || mCode == IC_POP_FRAME || mOperator == IA_FARXLAT) && !mConst.IsEqual(ins->mConst))
 		return false;
 
 	return true;
